<title>BELGIUM: Soros says G7 may hint at too fast dollar rise.</title>
<headline>Soros says G7 may hint at too fast dollar rise.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financier George Soros said on Thursday that the Group of Seven industrialised nations may suggest this weekend that the dollar's recent appreciation has been too fast.</p>
<p>Soros told Reuters: &quot;A strong dollar is in the interest of all parties....but the rate of change is too fast.&quot;  </p>
<p>When asked whether he though the G7 might suggest that the dollar's rise has been too rapid, Soros said: &quot;They might feel the same, but will be more diplomatic.&quot;</p>
<p>Soros was speaking after a meeting with European Commission President Jacques Santer about EU citizenship rights.</p>
</text>
